//! **Original addresses.** The REL is analysed at the synthetic base
//! `0x80A00000` (documented in `docs/REL.md` and `docs/REL2ELF.md`); the entry
//! point is `0x80A000F0`. Text ends at `0x80B2A518`, data occupies
//! `0x80B2A518..0x80B6E438`, and BSS starts at `0x80B6E500`. **None of these
//! are runtime addresses.** They are the canonical slots chosen by
//! `tools/rel2elf.mjs` so that the four REL images can be loaded together for
//! static analysis. Every function doc repeats the synthetic-base note.
//!
//! **Why it exists.** `d_enemiesNP` is where the game defines nearly every
//! enemy's `fState` records, its actor constructor and its AI callbacks. The
//! state tables are unusually strong evidence: the engine's own
//! `daEn<Class>_c::StateID_<Name>` strings survive in the data section, so the
//! role of each registration is known without guessing. Those names are the
//! backbone of this file.
//!
//! **Dependencies.** Only [`crate::platform`] (`read_u32`, `write_u32`,
//! `call0..call6`). Callees outside this file are addressed by their synthetic
//! REL address or by their `main.dol` address and are marked `// unknown:`
//! where their name is not established. No Nintendo symbol is invented.
