// ===========================================================================
// 14. Wave 12: `daEnBuku_c` per-state handlers and the `bakubaku`-model block
//
// This pass continues the two untranslated runs that wave 11 left behind:
//
// * `0x80A03150..0x80A03B10` - one `fState` callback, a small `0x528`-byte
//   actor constructor, two vtable helpers, the matrix/scale writer and the
//   model binder that loads `g3d/bakubaku.brres`. The binder is the anchor:
//   it names the model (`bakubaku`) and the clips (`swim`, `attack`) that the
//   surrounding code animates. The export carries no `StateID` table for this
//   actor, so the class label stays `unknown`.
// * `0x80A03E70..0x80A05970` - the `daEnBuku_c` per-state handler block. The
//   already-translated state table at `0x80A05500` installs the state objects
//   `0x80B6E7B8` (`Swim`), `0x80B6E7F8` (`SrcSwim`), `0x80B6E838`
//   (`AttackSwim`) and `0x80B6E878` (`AttackWait`); the four per-state
//   functions below jump to exactly those objects through vtable slot `+0xD4`.
//   The `0x1168`-byte `daEnBuku_c` constructor at `0x80A05CC0` already
//   documented the `+0x6D0..+0x6E0` slot words that the handlers use.
//
// Every address is a synthetic analysis address (base `0x80A00000`), not a
// runtime address.
//
// inferred: "per-state handler" means the body runs from one `fState` record's
// method slots. The export resolves those slots only through data that the
// loader relocates, so each handler is tied to its state by the state object
// it jumps to, not by a symbol.
// ===========================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Wave 12 data addresses used by the handlers below.
//
// The REL data section is relocated at load time, so every constant is read
// from its synthetic address instead of being baked in as a literal. The
// observed values are listed next to each address to make the arithmetic
// readable; they come from `work/rels/d_enemiesNP.rel` at offset
// `address - 0x80A00000`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Effect-manager word read by the four-word effect spawner (`0x80429F10`).
const DAT_80429F10: usize = 0x8042_9F10;

/// Frame-counter word tested with `& 7` by the `Swim` pitch wobble
/// (`0x8042A200`).
const DAT_8042A200: usize = 0x8042_A200;

/// Animation blend time handed to `0x801680E0` in the `bakubaku` binder
/// (`f32` 1.0 at this address).
const DAT_80B2A9A4: usize = 0x80B2_A9A4;

/// The actor block's neutral scalar (`f32` 0.0). Used as "zero" for floats and
/// vectors.
const DAT_80B2A994: usize = 0x80B2_A994;

/// Four-unit vertical offset (`f32` 4.0) inserted before reading a holder
/// matrix.
const DAT_80B2A9A0: usize = 0x80B2_A9A0;

/// `f32` 1.25, the chase speed multiplier passed to `0x80A04A90`.
