/// Main `gessoMini` frame handler.
///
/// While the engine word at `0x8042A200` has none of its low three bits set,
/// the body drifts the two speed words through the small tables at
/// `0x80B2D4B8`/`0x80B2D4C0`: the byte at `+0x5BF` selects the y direction
/// (`+/-0.0625` step to `-/+1.0`), the byte at `+0x5BE` the x direction. It
/// then integrates the speeds through `0x8006CD40`, adds the `0x800`
/// half-turn step to the `+0x102` angle (clamping a negative angle that
/// crosses zero), steps the animation holder, and counts the `+0x5C1`
/// lifetime byte down; at zero it calls the retire helper `0x80162510`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80a65f90` at `0x80A65F90` (300 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_enemiesNP/export/80a65f90_FUN_80a65f90.c`
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80A00000`; this is not a runtime address.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `actor` - `gessoMini` actor.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes `+0xEC`, `+0xE8`, `+0x102`, the two direction bytes and `+0x5C1`;
/// may retire the actor.
///
/// # Safety
/// The actor, its animation holder and the two tables must be valid.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - every branch and table index is explicit; the exact meaning of
/// the two direction bytes is inferred from the table contents.
