// 32. Wave 29: the rideable carrier (`0x80A921F0..0x80A92ED0`) and the
//     `jugem` platform actor (`0x80A93990..0x80A952D0`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// This pass continues at `0x80A921F0`, the first export after the wave-28
// `jugem`/`cloud_wait` binder, and covers two clusters.
//
// 1. `0x80A921F0..0x80A92ED0` - the per-frame steps of a *rideable carrier*.
//    The constructor of that class is outside the export, so the class name
//    is not printed anywhere; every role below is `// inferred:` from the
//    calls: `0x8005F900`/`0x8005FA60` resolve a player index, `0x80A92320`
//    returns the actor the carrier is touching, `0x80A923B0` steps the yaw
//    from that actor's x/z, and `0x80A91F40`/`0x80A91D70` are the two
//    untranslated neighbours from wave 28. `0x80A92E10`/`0x80A92ED0` copy a
//    player's transform onto the carrier and release it again, which is what
//    makes the "rideable" reading the only consistent one.
// 2. `0x80A93990..0x80A952D0` - the `jugem` platform actor. The asset name
//    `g3d/jugem.brres` (`0x80B50DA8`) and the clip table
//    `wait`/`throw_st`/`throw_wait`/`throw`/`dead`
//    (`0x80B50DC8..0x80B50DF0`, pointers at `0x80B50DF8`) identify it.
//    `0x80A93B10` is its `0x830`-byte constructor, `0x80A949B0` binds the
//    model and `0x80A94AD0` selects one of the five clips. The throw state
//    machine is `0x80A94EB0` plus the four small steps around it.
//
// Field map of the carrier block (every offset is observed in the export;
// the meanings follow the call shapes, `// inferred:`):
//
// | Offset | Meaning |
// |---|---|
// | `+0x060` | class vtable |
// | `+0x0AC..+0x0B4` | position X/Y/Z |
// | `+0x0DC/+0x0E0/+0x0E4` | horizontal speed triplet |
// | `+0x0E8` | current vertical speed |
// | `+0x0EC` | target vertical speed |
// | `+0x0F4` | facing word, `+2.0` or `-2.0` |
// | `+0x11C` | vertical acceleration clamp |
// | `+0x124` | byte driven by bit 1 of the `+0x722` flags |
// | `+0x348` | variant/facing byte copied from the player |
// | `+0x438` | short armed before the second attack descriptor |
// | `+0x548` | animation holder; slot `+0x1C` advances it |
// | `+0x6F8` | computed hover height |
// | `+0x6FC` | height clamp for the dive |
// | `+0x700` | per-frame height step |
// | `+0x704` | mode word tested before the second attack descriptor |
// | `+0x708` | state countdown |
// | `+0x70C` | player-lookup selector (`0` = `0x8005F900`) |
// | `+0x710` | "attached to a player" flag |
// | `+0x718` | up-step phase |
// | `+0x720` | aim timer |
// | `+0x722` | two-bit progress flags |
// | `+0x724` | "above the target height" byte |
// | `+0x726` | attached player index, `0xFF` = none |
// | `+0x727` | dive frame counter |
//
// Field map of the `jugem` block:
//
// | Offset | Meaning |
// |---|---|
// | `+0x148` | linked object, armed/released by `0x8008C330`/`0x8008C380` |
// | `+0x394` | class state object of the owning actor |
// | `+0x6EC..+0x6F4` | parent position copied by `0x80A947F0` |
// | `+0x72C` | first model holder |
// | `+0x748` | `jugem` resource |
// | `+0x74C` | first model/animation holder |
// | `+0x78C` | first clip holder |
// | `+0x7F4` | registry handle of the attached player object |
// | `+0x810` | fade timer |
// | `+0x818` | clip index selected by `0x80A94AD0` |
// | `+0x81C` | variant flag (`1` = the alternate spawn form) |
// | `+0x820` | retry countdown |
// | `+0x824` | "attached" flag |
// | `+0x828` | state-2 timer |
// | `+0x82C` | "released" flag |

