// ===========================================================================
// 47. Wave 67: the `0x80B03780..0x80B06120` rail/segment actor.
//
// This is one enemy that walks along a byte rail. It owns a **head** segment at
// `+0x540`, a **second** segment at `+0x6FC`, and up to `0x14` trailing
// segments at `+0x8B8` with stride `0x1B8`; the number of live trailing
// segments is the word at `+0x2B18`. Every segment holds
//
// | offset  | contents |
// |---|---|
// | `+0x000` | element vtable (`0x80B66718` for the head pair, `0x80B66724` otherwise) |
// | `+0x0A4` | `f32` position x |
// | `+0x0A8` | `f32` position y |
// | `+0x0AC` | `f32` position z |
// | `+0x0B0` | `f32` velocity/step x |
// | `+0x0B4` | `f32` velocity/step y |
// | `+0x0B8` | `f32` velocity/step z |
// | `+0x0BC` | committed rail point x |
// | `+0x0C0` | committed rail point y |
// | `+0x0C8` | model/animation holder |
// | `+0x198` | flag word (`1` = placed, `2` = follow-controller released) |
// | `+0x1AC` | current rail index |
// | `+0x1B0` | follow target (the actor the segment trails) |
// | `+0x1B4` | `u16` scratch counter |
//
// The block is covered in three runs: the class skeleton and the container
// constructor (`0x80B03780..0x80B03E20`), the segment-wide frame operations
// (`0x80B04A30..0x80B04E10`), and the position/timing helpers with the two
// per-frame integrators (`0x80B054D0..0x80B06120`).
//
// The class name is not printed anywhere in this run of the export, so the
// actor is described by allocation size (`0x2B40`) and offsets only. The
// vtables are literal: `0x80B66498` (written at `+0x60`), `0x80B66718` (head
// element) and `0x80B66724` (base element).
// ===========================================================================

