// 52. Wave 72: the `0x80AB0000` bucket continuation
// ===========================================================================
//
// Two contiguous runs of the `0x80AB0000` bucket, both reconstructed from
// clean exports (no QGPR save/restore pseudo-code, no `halt_baddata`).
//
// The first run, `0x80AB7810..0x80AB9030`, opens with the tail of the
// five-entry state-descriptor skeleton that the earlier waves established: the
// `:`-suffix name predicate at `0x80AB7810`, the two 48-byte argument-swapping
// forwarders at `0x80AB78D0`/`0x80AB7900` and the `0x770`-byte constructor at
// `0x80AB7930`. The rest of the run is the presentation and step surface of
// the objects around that constructor. No class name is printed anywhere in
// this run, and the offsets do not all fit one object (`0x80AB8A60` uses
// `+0x850`/`+0x854` while the constructor allocates only `0x770` bytes), so
// the run is described by size, offsets and its literal resource names:
//
// - `0x80AB7F40` spawns the named effect `Wm_en_kuribobigsplit` (`0x80B55E80`),
// - `0x80AB85D0` binds the `lift_buranko` model from `g3d/lift_buranko.brres`,
// - `0x80AB8290` starts the `walk` clip on both clip holders,
// - `0x80AB9030` binds the `jump_st` clip,
// - `0x80AB8E30..0x80AB8FE0` work on the two 0x30-byte holders at
//   `+0x5EC`/`+0x61C` and emit effect family `0x73` from one of them.
//
// Field map of the `0x770`-byte object built by [`fn_80ab7930`]:
//
// - `+0x60` class vtable, written as `0x80304E10` and then overwritten with
//   `0x80B55E98`,
// - `+0x524` model holder (reset by `0x80069020`, finished by `0x800690E0`),
// - `+0x540` model record, `+0x544` first clip holder (`0x80169CD0`),
// - `+0x584` second clip holder (`0x80168D10`, vtable `0x80B330E0`),
// - `+0x5C0` sub-object vtable `0x803295D8` (replaced by `0x80329548`),
// - `+0x5CC` sub-object (`0x8016A5E0`),
// - `+0x5F0` sub-object installed by `0x802D7AA0`, vtable `0x80329958`,
// - `+0x704..+0x714` zeroed flag/counter words.
//
// Offsets the later helpers add to that picture: `+0xAC..+0xB4` position
// vector, `+0xDC` scale vector, `+0xE8..+0xF0` speed/scale triple, `+0x348`
// side byte, `+0x391` effect group byte, `+0x2DC` owned object handle,
// `+0x5EC`/`+0x61C` the two animation holders, `+0x718` owner word and
// `+0x850`/`+0x854` the phase word plus its countdown.
//
// The second run, `0x80ABB3D0..0x80ABBCF8`, is the `lift_zen_toge` lift actor
// (the `g3d/lift_zen_toge.brres` model and `lift_zen_toge` node are literal in
