// 64. Wave 84: the `0x80AC0000` bucket's later runs
//
// Three runs in the same bucket, all still inside the world-map actor band:
//
// * `0x80AC2220..0x80AC3B24` - the state steps of the `mecha_koopa` actor that
//   wave 55 only opened (binder `0x80AC16D0`, matrix rebuild `0x80AC1920`).
//   They share one shape: release the `+0x5C0` and `+0x548` holders through
//   their `+0x14`/`+0x1C` slots, run the frame helpers, and switch state
//   through the class vtable slot `+0xD4` with one of the four region objects
//   at `0x80B759A0`, `0x80B759E0`, `0x80B75A20` or `0x80B75B20`.
// * `0x80AC4B50..0x80AC5D00` - the actor that opens `g3d/met.brres` and keeps
//   its model holder at `+0x7F8`, its animation holder at `+0x7FC` and the
//   second holder at `+0x83C`. Its frame steps gate on the `+0x274` button
//   word and on the `+0x348` side byte, and it re-enters its approach step
//   `0x80AC4C40` from two of them.
// * `0x80ACF450..0x80ACF7D0` - a sixth copy of the descriptor skeleton already
//   translated in waves 46, 53, 54, 55, 69 and 77: two normalisers, one
//   constant producer, the `+0x30` chain walker, the `:`-suffix name predicate
//   and the two 48-byte deleting-destructor forwarders.
//
// `0x80AC1800` and `0x80AC0750` stay untranslated: their exports still carry
// unresolved `unaff_GQR0` paired-single artifacts, so the float arguments
// cannot be reconstructed honestly. They are called from this pass by address
// with a note, exactly as wave 55 did. `0x80AC0840` was resolved in wave 152 as
// [`fn_80ac0840`] (`qr3` pinned to `GQR3 = 0x00050005`).
