// 69. Wave 88 - the `0x80AF0000` bucket's ghost and upside-down-spiky tails
//
// The bucket was opened by waves 48 and 73 (the `obj_tobira` door block, the
// `daEnRotBlock_c` helpers and the `daEnRotarionGhost_c` block). This pass
// takes two runs that were still untranslated.
//
// `0x80AF6190..0x80AF7330` is the `Wm_en_teresa` world-map ghost. Its class
// is named by the strings it hands to the resource and clip lookups:
// `teresa` at `0x80B6404C`, `fog` at `0x80B64054` and `Wm_en_teresatail` at
// `0x80B64058`. The actor keeps the `+0x524`/`+0x540`/`+0x544` holder chain,
// a second `+0x584` animation holder and the `+0x790` material holder, and
// reads its clip names from the two per-variant pointer tables at
// `0x80B63FB0` and `0x80B64014`.
//
// `0x80AF8660..0x80AF9EF0` is the five-entry state-descriptor skeleton and
// the same-actor surface of two classes. The skeleton has two normalisers,
// two `+0x30` chain walkers, the `:`-suffix name predicate, two
// `0x802DCBFC` deleting-destructor forwarders and the constructor it fronts.
// The first constructor is the `0x9D8`-byte `daEnSakasaTogezo_c` actor
// (vtable `0x80B647FC`); its state table is
// [`register_sakasa_togezo_states`] (translated earlier), which names the
// records `0x80B77CB0` (`Saka_`), `0x80B77CF0` (second `Saka_`) and
// `0x80B77D2C` (`Slid_`). The slide entry and the two per-frame handlers
// here dispatch exactly those three records. The second constructor opens
// the following `0x800`-byte sibling (vtable `0x80B64CB8`).
