// ===========================================================================
// 71. Wave 90: the `killer_mag` actor (`0x80AA62A0..0x80AA9350`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// One `0xA20`-byte actor class occupies this run. Its constructor installs
// class vtable `0x80B53A80` and the virtual entry at slot `+0x08` of that
// vtable is `0x80AA67A0` (the spawn initialiser below). The model binder at
// `0x80AA86C0` loads the two variants `killer_mag` / `g3d/killer_mag.brres`
// and `killer` / `g3d/killer.brres` from the tables at `0x80B53998`,
// `0x80B539D0` and `0x80B539D8`, and the spawn initialiser selects four of
// the records that [`register_killer_states`] names
// `daEnKiller_c::StateID_MagMove` (`0x80B74C10`), `Move` (`0x80B74C50`),
// `SearchMove` (`0x80B74C90`) and `SearchMagM` (`0x80B74CD0`). The run is
// therefore the `killer_mag` half of that family: it shares the state table
// and the `+0x414` attack-record shape with [`alloc_killer_actor`]'s class,
// but not its size (`0xA20` here) or its class vtable (`0x80B54118` there).
//
// Layout (byte offsets into the actor):
//   `+0x4FC` collision mask, `+0x348` side byte, `+0x38F` layer, `+0x45D`
//   last side-probe flag, `+0x40`/`+0x90`/`+0x94` player-side words,
//   `+0x524` model-holder context, `+0x540` model pointer, `+0x544` model
//   record, `+0x584`/`+0x5C0`/`+0x5EC` animation holders, `+0x618`/`+0x740`
//   `0x802D7AA0` helpers (vtable `0x80329958`), `+0x868` animator and
//   `+0x8C4` render block.
//   `+0x9CC` saved state word, `+0x9D4` spin mode, `+0x9DC` variant nibble,
//   `+0x9E0`/`+0x9E4` spawn bits, `+0x9E8` variant count, `+0x9EC` sub-state,
//   `+0x9F0` loop count, `+0x9F4` model-variant flag (0 = `killer_mag`,
//   1 = `killer`), `+0x9FC` spin accumulator, `+0xA00`/`+0xA06`/`+0xA08`/
//   `+0xA0A` countdowns, `+0xA0C` arm flag, `+0xA12`/`+0xA14` roll offset,
//   `+0xA16` roll direction, `+0xA17` saved direction, `+0xA18` last splash
//   mask.
//   `+0x414..+0x432` the attack/hit record: five words, two bytes and the
//   `+0x432` valid flag.
//
