// 72. Wave 91: the `dossun` and `jugem` blocks of the `0x80A50000` bucket
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Three runs, all inside the bucket that the wave-78 pass opened
// (`0x80A50430..0x80A52D60`) and before the wave-19/20 `FireSnake`/`gabon`
// material (`0x80A5AE30` onwards):
//
// * `0x80A51A30..0x80A521F0` - the third `0x6E8`-byte copy of the five-entry
//   state-descriptor skeleton (deleting destructor, constant producer
//   `0x80358084`, `+0x30` chain walker, `:`-suffix name predicate and the two
//   48-byte forwarders), the matching `0x6E8` constructor with class vtable
//   `0x80B44DEC`, and one delta-position helper that reads a 3x4 matrix.
// * `0x80A53710..0x80A54120` - the `dossun` actor (the Thwomp-family enemy;
//   inferred from the model names `dossun`/`dossun_big`): its
//   `g3d/dossun.brres` model binder, the landing-effect emitter with the three
//   `Wm_en_dossunfall0N` names, the spin/turn timer, the two "clip finished ->
//   next state" steps, the wall/ground contact dispatcher and the two state
//   entries that fire sounds `0x211`/`0x212` and `0x20F`/`0x210`. The single
//   gap at `0x80A53850` is listed in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE91_ENEMIES.md`.
// * `0x80A54C00..0x80A55220` - the `0x5F0`-byte `jugem` actor: the five-entry
//   skeleton that fronts it (two deleting destructors, the constant producers
//   `0x80358004` and `0x80357BF4`, the chain walker, the name predicate and two
//   forwarders), its constructor with class vtable `0x80B45B20`, the transform
//   commit and the `g3d/jugem.brres` + `jugem`/`throw` binder.
//
// Field map shared by the `dossun` handlers (all offsets literal in the
// exports):
//
// | offset | role |
// |---|---|
// | `+0xEC` | state timer word written by the state entries |
// | `+0x100`/`+0x102` | the two halfword angles cleared by [`fn_80a54120`] |
// | `+0x114` | per-variant speed word |
// | `+0x148` | embedded object refreshed by `0x8008C380` |
// | `+0x1EC` | the physics/collision block every probe uses |
// | `+0x500` | halfword state id (`0x0D` in the wait entry) |
// | `+0x524`/`+0x540`/`+0x544`/`+0x584` | model-holder context, model resource, model record, animation holder |
// | `+0x5B8` | mode byte raised to `3` late in the fall |
// | `+0x5D0` | variant: `0` is `dossun`, `1` is `dossun_big` |
// | `+0x5D4` | contact mode tested by [`fn_80a53e70`] |
// | `+0x5DC` | countdown byte used by three of the state steps |
//
// All constants below were read from `work/rels/elf/d_enemiesNP.elf`; the
// strings at `0x80B454D0`..`0x80B45564` and `0x80B45B00`..`0x80B45B18` were
// dumped from that image, and the float words are quoted with their values.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

