// ===========================================================================
// 79. Wave 98: the `basabasa` actor of the `0x80A00000` bucket
//     (`0x80A0A240..0x80A0C470`)
//
// This is one complete actor of twenty-eight binary functions, twenty-six of
// which are translated here. The class name does not survive: the model strings
// (`g3d/basabasa.brres`, `basabasa`, `basabasa_wait`, `basabasa_fly`) are the
// only printable identity, and the class vtable at `0x80B348E8` is referenced
// only by the constructor. The actor is therefore described by vtable, size and
// field offsets.
//
// Field map established from the constructor and the three model binders:
//
//   * `+0x524` model/animation block, `+0x540` wait model, `+0x544` fly model,
//     `+0x548` eye model (`basa_eye_light`);
//   * `+0x54C` wait animation holder, `+0x58C` fly holder, `+0x69C` eye holder;
//   * `+0x5CC`/`+0x604`/`+0x6DC` the three clip records of those holders;
//   * `+0x63C`/`+0x640` wait animation + controller, `+0x66C`/`+0x670` fly
//     animation + controller, `+0x714`/`+0x718` eye animation + controller;
//   * `+0x348` side byte (0 = target on the right, 1 = target on the left),
//     `+0x360` state word, `+0x74C` latched player slot (`0xFF` = none),
//     `+0x750` eye-enabled word, `+0x75C` latched target handle;
//   * `+0x100/+0x102/+0x104` the three halfword angles, `+0x7C` matrix,
//     `+0xAC/+0xB0/+0xB4` position, `+0xDC` position vector.
//
// `+0x750` gates every eye-model operation and also selects the 80.0 / 128.0
// grab radius in [`fn_80a0ba80`]; whether it means "has eyes" or "is the
// larger variant" is not established, so the docs keep it neutral.
//
// Two bodies in the same run are NOT translated: `0x80A0B8A0` (a target search
// whose export renders the loop as a two-argument recursive call to itself, so
// neither its signature nor its chaining call can be read honestly) and
// `0x80A0BD20` (its caller, which would need that untranslated signature).
// `0x80A0A530`, `0x80A0AB20`, `0x80A0AB70`, `0x80A0ACB0`, `0x80A0ACC0` and
// `0x80A0C8D0` are referenced from the class vtable but have no entry in
// `functions.tsv`, so no byte count exists for them and they are out of scope.
