// ===========================================================================
// 93. Wave 112: the `0x80A00000` bucket continuation
// ===========================================================================
//
// Three groups close out the low end of this REL:
//
// * `0x80A00200` and `0x80A00240` - two 64-byte deleting helpers of the base
//   enemy framework. They only run the heap release `0x802B9280` and return
//   the pointer, so the caller can chain the free. `0x80A00200` is also the
//   function pointer that [`fn_80a70b00`] hands to the `0x802DC7E0` element
//   container as its per-element hook.
// * `0x80A08CB0..0x80A09880` - ten per-state steps of an actor that carries a
//   linked list of *rider* objects and copies the rider's player slot into its
//   own state. The list hangs off `+0x588` (node payload at `+0x04`, next node
//   at `+0x0C`); a rider counts only while its `+0x38C` byte is `1`. The steps
//   drive the actor's own vertical offset `+0xEC`, the ride height `+0x550`
//   and the collision flags at `+0x5B4`. Ghidra prints the shared probe
//   `0x80A08DC0` without arguments at several call sites; the probe's own body
//   reads its `this` in `r3`, so every call passes the actor.
// * `0x80A0D5B0..0x80A0E3B0` - the `kuriboMini` (Mini Goomba) actor, seventeen
//   of its state steps. The model binder at `0x80A0DDD0` loads
//   `g3d/kuriboMini.brres` and binds the `kuriboMini` node, and it initialises
//   exactly the `+0x524`/`+0x544`/`+0x584` holders that the `0x618`-byte
//   constructor of wave 83 ([`fn_80a0d350`]) sets up, so both belong to one
//   class. The block holds a matrix refresh, five sound wrappers (events
//   `0x1F9`..`0x1FC`), a contact handler, the six-button stomp counter and the
//   three frame steps around the `+0x1EC` ground query.
// ===========================================================================

// --- Callees, cited by analysis address. ---

/// Transforms a world position by the three-angle triple at `+0x100`.
const EN112_FN_80064AF0: usize = 0x8006_4AF0;
/// Builds the `+0x7C` matrix from a position triple.
