/// Deleting helper of the base enemy framework.
///
/// The body is the smallest form of the family teardown: only a positive
/// `mode` releases the object, and the pointer is always returned.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80a00200` at `0x80A00200` (64 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_enemiesNP/export/80a00200_FUN_80a00200.c`
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80A00000`; this is not a runtime address.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this` - object to release; may be null.
/// - `mode` - positive to also return the object to the heap.
///
/// # Returns
/// `this`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// For a positive `mode`, runs the heap release `0x802B9280(this)`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be a live object or null.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the guard, the release and the returned pointer are literal.
pub unsafe fn fn_80a00200(this: usize, mode: i32) -> usize {
    if this != 0 && mode > 0 {
        call1(FN_802B9280, this as u32);
    }
    this
}

/// Second copy of the deleting helper above; only the address differs.
