// 97. Wave 116: the `bilikyu` world-map enemy and the `0x730`-byte
//     `0x80A10000`-bucket actor (0x80A19A70..0x80A1A3A0 and
//     0x80A1C790..0x80A1DAD0)
//
// Two runs of the `0x80A10000` bucket:
//
// * `0x80A19A70..0x80A1A3A0` - the `Wm_en_birikyu` world-map enemy. The
//   `0x80A19A70` binder opens `g3d/bilikyu.brres`, resolves the `bilikyu` node
//   three times (model, matrix holder and animation holder) and starts the
//   `body_wait` clip; `0x80A19DF0` rebuilds the actor matrix from the position
//   triple plus the `+0x724` bob offset and commits it to the `+0x544` holder;
//   `0x80A19EE0` is the triangle-wave bob stepper over `+0x720`/`+0x724`;
//   `0x80A1A200` and `0x80A1A300` bind `body_wait` and `body_stop`; the
//   `0x80A19BD0` retire path tests the `0x80358004` (`InIceLump`) state and
//   emits the `0x1CE` effect; `0x80A1A150` is the contact callback and
//   `0x80A1A3A0` the `+0x71C` countdown that switches state when it expires.
// * `0x80A1C790..0x80A1DAD0` - one `0x730`-byte actor whose state word sits at
//   `+0x800`, whose variant word sits at `+0x804`, whose four-player slot bytes
//   sit at `+0x66C..+0x66F` and whose `+0x81A` angle drives the two thumbnail
//   helpers `0x80A1CEA0`/`0x80A1CF30`. The run covers the byte-table getter,
//   the turn/limit step, the four `0x80064610` message senders, the stage
//   position/`0x80077860` update, the `+0x800` dispatcher `0x80A1D130`, its two
//   wrapper steps and the `0x730`-byte allocator `0x80A1DAD0`.
