// ===========================================================================
// 102. Wave 121: the `0x80A70000` bucket remainder
//     (`0x80A70E20..0x80A71F40`, `0x80A74570..0x80A754B0`,
//      `0x80A7A170..0x80A7AEF0` and `0x80A7D030..0x80A7DCC0`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// Wave 120 took the `0x80AB0000` bucket, so the `0x80A70000` bucket still held
// 58 untranslated functions. This pass takes four of its clusters:
//
// **The two chain actors' walk steps (`0x80A70E20..0x80A71F40`).** The
// `0x868`/`0x988`-byte segmented actors of wave 14 keep their segment count at
// `+0x540`, the first segment at `+0x544` and the next segment at `+0x238`.
// Four of the seven bodies below run that loop directly. `0x80A715E0` and
// `0x80A71700`
// start the `walk_normal` and `walk_angly` clips on every segment and are
// byte-for-byte the same shape as the wave-85 `fn_80a10730`, which is what
// fixes both the frame arrays and the two clip names. `0x80A71AA0` and
// `0x80A71F40` are the per-frame handlers of the two classes and share the
// heading update [`fn_80a70f40`]; `0x80A71F40` adds the `+0x944` turn
// countdown. `0x80A71C60` is the effect-plus-turn step that follows them.
//
// **The `daEnHimanBros_c` jump-clip block (`0x80A74570..0x80A754B0`).** Wave
// 16 left the shared clip player `0x80A74570` untranslated and called it by
// address. This pass translates it, so [`fn_80a74570`] now expands the four
// arguments of every call site: `(blend frame, actor, clip name, attach
// flag)`. The seven entries after it are the `jump`/`jump_ed`/`jump_attack`
// state entries of the class whose state table is `0x80A75800`; their clip
// names (`jump_st`, `jump_ed`, `jump_attack`, `jump_attack_ed`) and the four
// per-side names (`throw_L/R`, `jump_throw_L/R`) are read from the REL image
// and quoted in the bodies.
//
// **The `0xEB0` actor's placement helpers (`0x80A7A170..0x80A7AEF0`).** Six
// helpers of the `0xEB0`-byte object block of section 19: the per-node
// placement recompute over the node-id table `0x80B2E068`, the clip-rate speed
// helper and the `+0xE7C` countdown pair, the per-side placement offset and
// the `0x16`-node x-extent probe.
//
// **The `daEnIcicle_c` descriptor skeleton (`0x80A7D030..0x80A7DCC0`).** The
// two constant producers, four 48-byte state-destructor forwarders (two before
// and two after the `0x628`-byte `daEnIcicle_c` constructor `0x80A7DCF0`) and
// the class's three-phase frame handler `0x80A7D760`.
//
// **Address convention.** Every address here is the synthetic analysis address
// of `tools/rel2elf.mjs` (base `0x80A00000`); a REL stores no load address, so
// none of them is a runtime address.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Wave 121 constants
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

