// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 0x800279F0 - release the three embedded coin-family holders
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Releases the three embedded holders at `+0x7AC`, `+0x7EC` and `+0x89C`.
///
/// In plain English: each holder is its own interface object, so the body
/// loads the holder's vtable, reads the release slot and calls it with the
/// holder address as receiver. The first two use slot `+0x1C`, the third uses
/// slot `+0x14`. This is the `main.dol` tail target of [`fn_80a3f6d0`], whose
/// `+0xA90` word gates the teardown of the coin-family actor.
///
/// # Original (untabled)
/// - Ghidra: none - no `functions.tsv` row for `0x800279F0`.
/// - Extent: `0x800279F0..0x80027A54` (100 bytes, 25 words), ending at the
///   `blr` at `0x80027A50`; three zero words follow at
///   `0x80027A54..0x80027A60` and the next body starts at `0x80027A60`.
/// - Reach: no `b`/`bl` in the main image; `d_enemiesNP` reaches it through
///   the tail branch `b@0x80A3F6DC` inside [`fn_80a3f6d0`]. No data word names
///   it.
/// - Observed: `9421FFF0 stwu r1,-0x10(r1)`; `mflr r0`; `stw r0,0x14(r1)`;
///   `stw r31,0xC(r1)`; `mr r31,r3`; `lwz r12,0x7AC(r3)`;
///   `lwz r12,0x1C(r12)`; `mtspr CTR,r12`; `addi r3,r3,0x7AC`;
///   `4E800421 bcctrl 20,0` (call); `lwz r12,0x7EC(r31)`;
///   `addi r3,r31,0x7EC`; `lwz r12,0x1C(r12)`; `mtspr CTR,r12`;
///   `4E800421 bcctrl 20,0`; `lwz r12,0x89C(r31)`;
///   `addi r3,r31,0x89C`; `lwz r12,0x14(r12)`; `mtspr CTR,r12`;
///   `4E800421 bcctrl 20,0`; epilogue; `4E800020 blr`.
/// - Decoder note: all three `4E800421` words are calls that fall through;
///   the descent therefore counts three calls and still ends on one `blr`.
/// - Evidence: `work/wave285/e_dis.txt`, `work/wave285/e_refs.txt`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: coin-family actor whose three holder blocks are constructed.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Three virtual release calls on the embedded holders.
///
/// # Safety
/// `+0x7AC`, `+0x7EC` and `+0x89C` must hold live interface objects whose
/// vtable slots `+0x1C`/`+0x1C`/`+0x14` are callable.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the three vtable loads, slot offsets and receiver adjustments are
/// literal.
pub unsafe fn fn_800279f0(this: usize) {
    for (offset, slot) in [(0x7ACusize, 0x1Cusize), (0x7EC, 0x1C), (0x89C, 0x14)] {
        let holder = this + offset;
        let vtable = platform::read_u32(holder) as usize;
        call1(platform::read_u32(vtable + slot) as usize, holder as u32);
    }
}

