// ===========================================================================
// 123. Wave 141: the eleven "ready" `docs/SPEC_WAVE140_ENEMIES.md` bodies and
//      six `0x80AC0000` planner-bucket rows
// ===========================================================================
//
// Section-local adapters and constants only; every address below is a synthetic
// analysis address (base `0x80A00000`) or a `main.dol` address, and none of them
// is a runtime address. Every out-of-image callee was confirmed from the REL's
// module-0 `R_PPC_REL24` import stream, not from the raw branch displacement
// (the Ghidra exports truncate at every out-of-image `b`/`bl`).
//
// **The `qr3` loads.** Each `psq_l fD,0(rA),1,qr3` in this section reads the
// `u16` staged two instructions earlier. `GQR3 = 0x00050005` is an unsigned
// 16-bit type at scale 0 (`docs/REL_ELF_MAPPING.md`), so every such site is
// written as `(f32)*(u16*)`. The `psq_st fN,..,qr0` prologue saves are plain FPR
// spills and stay as `stfd` in the original; they need no port.
//
// **The `2^52 + 2^31` bias.** The `0x43300000`/`xoris` sequences convert a
// signed integer to `f32`. The bias cancels exactly (and, for the Q12 pair at
// `0x80AA36F8`, cancels modulo `2^16` after the `fctiwz`/`sth` truncation), so
// the ports write the converted value directly and say so per site.

// --- Callees cited by analysis address --------------------------------------

