// --- 129b.5 `0x80AB0EE0` five-slot world-matrix refresh ---------------------

/// Rebuilds the actor's world matrix and publishes it to one or five holders.
///
/// With `+0x99B == 0` the body composes the `+0x7C` matrix from the position
/// `+0xAC..+0xB4` and rotation `+0x100/0x102/0x104`, publishes it to the
/// `+0x544` holder and copies three bone translations into `+0x884..0x8B0`.
/// Otherwise it repeats the same composition for four 12-byte records at
/// `+0x8CC` and angle triples at `+0x93E` into the five `+0x584` holders
/// (stride `0x40`); only the first slot publishes a bone.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80ab0ee0` at `0x80AB0EE0` (640 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_enemiesNP/export/80ab0ee0_FUN_80ab0ee0.c`
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80A00000`; this is not a runtime address.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: the actor; `+0x99B` mode byte, `+0x7C` matrix, `+0x544` holder,
///   `+0x8CC` record array, `+0x93E` angle array.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Rewrites `+0x7C`, publishes it into one or four holders and writes the
/// bone translations.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` and every holder must be constructed.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - both modes, the record/angle strides and the `i == 1` bone publish
/// are literal. The export's stack-slot names for the bone buffer are a
/// Ghidra artefact: the raw stream passes `r1+0x78` (mode A) and `r1+0x48`
/// (mode B) and reads the translation column at `+0xC/+0x1C/+0x2C`.
