// --- 130b.10 `0x80A06560` four-slot attachment placement (`qr3`) ------------

/// Places up to four attached actors relative to this actor.
///
/// Each of the four registry ids at `+0x738 + i*4` is resolved through
/// `0x80162D00` and skipped when the target's `+0x5BC` gate is clear. In circle
/// mode (`+0x1162 == 0`) the target is stepped toward a point on a `16.0`
/// circle at `+0x115E + table[target.+0x5C0]` with rate and dead-band `0.125`,
/// then the actor's three angles are copied. In record mode the target follows
/// the `+0x74C` record entry `target.+0x5C0 + 1` and only the `+0x102` angle
/// comes from this actor.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80a06560` at `0x80A06560` (500 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_enemiesNP/export/80a06560_FUN_80a06560.c`
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80A00000`; this is not a runtime address.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: the placer; `+0x738` id table, `+0x115E` base angle, `+0x1154`/
///   `+0x1158` step limits, `+0x1162` mode byte, `+0x74C` record table.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Moves each attachment through [`fn_80a65ce0`] and writes its three angles.
///
/// # Safety
/// The target ids, the record table and both actors must be live.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the two `qr3` sites are `(f32)(u16)`; the raw `bc 12,2` at
/// `0x80A065E4` confirms `+0x1162 == 0` is the circle mode, the reverse of the
/// export's branch nesting.
