// `docs/UNTABLED_POINTER_TABLES.md` lists `0x80314068` as a tier-3 "`dEn_c`
// enemy base-state table (306 slots)". Decoding the run says something both
// smaller and stronger:
//
// * `0x80314068..0x80314530` is 306 code words, but they are the **method half
//   of one CodeWarrior vtable**. The header is the two zero words at
//   `0x80314060`/`0x80314064` - the same `{0, 0}` layout as the player-family
//   vtables `0x8030F1D8`/`0x8030F228` documented in `src/game/player.rs`.
//   Word `0x80314530` is zero, then the next vtable starts at `0x80314534`.
// * The vtable address `0x80314060` (not `0x80314068`) is installed at object
//   offset `+0x60` by the two constructors at `0x800A88A0`
//   (`lis r3,0x8031; addi r3,r3,0x4060; stw r3,0x60(r27)`) and `0x800A8B10`
//   (`lis r4,0x8031; addi r4,r4,0x4060; stw r4,0x60(r3)`), so virtual dispatch
//   is `[[object + 0x60] + 0x8 + 4*n]` and method `n` is word `n` of the run the
//   audit started one slot late. That also explains why the wave-227 scan found
//   no reference to the reported base: every caller names `0x80314060`.
// * `0x800AED54` additionally treats `0x80314060` as a static-record base and
//   copies the words at `+0x690`, `+0x69C` and `+0x6A8`, i.e. the same block
