// `..._Break` sit at `0x80323A00..0x80323A7C`, immediately after the
// twelve-entry state record block that follows this array. The surrounding
// model data names the `g3d/ice.brres` archive and the `ice_A1`..`ice_C2`
// variants.
//
// Four shipped facts fix the identity:
//
// * the header is materialised by `lis r4,0x8032` / `addi r4,r4,0x3890` at
//   `0x80114AEC`/`0x80114AF8` and stored with `stw r4,0x60(r30)` at
//   `0x80114AFC` inside [`crate::game::worldmap::fn_80114ac0`];
// * the state names below the array spell `daEnemyIce_c::StateID_*`;
// * the twelve state records are four groups of three functions
//   (`{init, execute, end}` per named state), and the first record of each
//   group (`0x80115240`, `0x801152E0`, `0x80115350`, `0x80115420`) sits in the
//   `0x80114xxx`/`0x80115xxx` `daEnemyIce_c` method band;
// * slot 16 is the deleting destructor for the same `0x6B8`-byte object:
//   it releases `+0x58C`, `+0x460`, `+0x434`, `+0x3F0` and `+0x3D0`, the five
//   members the constructor builds, then runs the base release `0x800671B0`.
//
